window.location = window.location;

Next I’d write some JavaScript code to detect whenever the user clicks or uses any sort of keyboard or mouse input to cause the browser to navigate to a new URL.

window.onblur = function() {
    // Is this the current URL?  If so, do nothing
    if (window.location.href == window.location.href)
        return;

    // Otherwise, compare against the current URL
    window.location.href = window.location.href;
};

